# graphql-on-get.tflw — CHECK-ONLY FIXTURE (tflw `M242` `C`, `D1328`): a `body graphql` on a `GET`
# — `TF085`. The body kind is GraphQL-over-HTTP's POST shape; on a `GET` the query is a body most
# servers ignore, so the response would answer nothing that was asked. The repair is the method.
#
# Run explicitly (dot-directory — see bad-keyword.tflw's header for why):
#   npx tflw check tests/.checkonly/graphql-on-get.tflw
test "a GraphQL query sent the wrong way"
  api GET /graphql body graphql "{ products { id } }"
  expect status equals 200
